conclusion: dwell = B / r has no finite supremum over the set of workloads the fill-only-triggered policy must tolerate (r -> 0 gives dwell -> infinity for ANY fixed B); this is provable directly from the stated flush policy, the 18 sampled points in the round-2 report are a numerical calibration of this formula, not the basis for the no-bound claim -- the no-bound claim is stronger than 'extrapolation', it is a closed-form consequence.
